    {
        "content": "<p>I just opened <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15053\">lean#15053</a>. I think this was mentioned before, but I cannot find any discussion about it (either in lean4 issues or on Zulip).</p>\n<p>In the examples below, put your cursor on the line above the <code>^</code>. These places show the wrong tactic state.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hAB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">--^</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">shown:</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">A B C : Prop</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">hA : A</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">hAB : A ∧ B</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">⊢ A ↔ C</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\">expected:</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">A B C : Prop</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">hA : A</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">⊢ B</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">--^</span>\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">shown:</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">this : True</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">⊢ False</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\">expected:</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">⊢ True</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is annoying, because those are the expected places where the next tactic is written.</p>",
        "id": 622326735,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1788798763
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, I didn't look through closed issues. Is this a recent regression?<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/1927\">lean#1927</a> is exactly the same as this issue, and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14394\">lean#14394</a> is similar.</p>",
        "id": 622329871,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1788799190
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it used to pick up on which column your cursor is in, but since recently it doesn't do that anymore</p>",
        "id": 622338576,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788801875
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the problem comes from <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/11958\">lean4#11958</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This PR adjusts the elaborator and snapshot tree system so as not to rerun tactics when whitespace directly following them is changed, [...] We do this by removing the trailing whitespace before passing a tactic from the tactic block elaborator to <code>evalTactic</code>. [...]</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>So I think the nested block inside of the <code>have</code> tactic doesn't have trailing whitespace information but the <code>have</code> tactic itself keeps it so we get the information about after the <code>have</code> tactic at that position.</p>",
        "id": 622344127,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788803845
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The PR description also says</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The removed whitespace is saved in the snapshot tree and reapplied on access such that no consumers have to be adapted.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>but it seems like this isn't quite true; the info trees don't seem to keep the same trailing whitespace as they had before.</p>",
        "id": 622344327,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788803920
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(at least that's my guess without looking at the code)</p>",
        "id": 622344386,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788803943
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Did <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15095\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15095</a> fix this? (It didn't say <code>Closes:</code>)</p>",
        "id": 623710256,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1789196152
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this is fixed by <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15093\">lean#15093</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15095\">lean#15095</a>.</p>",
        "id": 623720200,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1789203111
    }
